{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3071","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3071","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3071\",\"parent_revision\":\"11ca44b58b1b2f9fd5a1f4e8981f133ac0439476943d2183e7494f65fb58982c\",\"root_revision\":\"11ca44b58b1b2f9fd5a1f4e8981f133ac0439476943d2183e7494f65fb58982c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe doc's title, filename, and one internal line still assert an MCP-specific scope that the\\narchitecture explicitly rejects: `dh_core` is the shared operations layer behind both the MCP\\ntool and the CLI (see `docs/component-architecture.md`, \\\"Where workflow is described\\\"), and\\n`docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md` is normative \\\"across every transport \u2014 MCP and\\nCLI alike\\\" (already corrected in the doc body via #3053).\\n\\nRemaining scope-mismatch after #3053's content fix:\\n\\n- Filename: `mcp-progressive-disclosure-contract.md`\\n- Title: \\\"MCP Progressive-Disclosure Contract\\\"\\n- Self-description: \\\"This document describes the shipped contract \u2014 what agents observe.\\\"\\n  (no transport qualifier on that line, though the surrounding paragraph is now transport-neutral)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Why This Was Left Alone\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nDeferred during the #2956/#3054 architecture session on the assumption that renaming would\\nbreak inbound links. That assumption does not hold: exactly 4 in-repo files reference this\\nfilename, no external links exist.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Inbound References To Update In The Same Change\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md`\\n- `.claude/agent-memory/dh-service-docs-maintainer/unenforced-map-guarantee.md`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Suggested Fix\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. `git mv docs/mcp-progressive-disclosure-contract.md docs/progressive-disclosure-contract.md`\\n   (or another transport-neutral name \u2014 final name is an open call, not this issue's decision)\\n2. Update the H1 title to drop \\\"MCP\\\"\\n3. Update the 4 inbound links above\\n4. Update the self-description line to name both transports, or drop the qualifier entirely\\n   since the doc already states in its own header that it's mechanical reference \\\"on one\\n   conforming implementation\\\" (the MCP tool) with a pointer to `backend-providers.md` for CLI\\n   parity \u2014 decide whether that stays MCP-specific-by-design (documents one implementation) or\\n   becomes dual-transport.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope Note\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThis is a naming/framing fix only. It does not change #3063 (CLI cannot reach address-based\\nnavigation) \u2014 that's the actual capability gap this doc's title has been mistaken for.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f279204221f5f4479f2ccc33ef1c56f46dfa19fbe1f318d9802e9fd66d40951e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvcMNw\"}"}